moderate","evidence":["Petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; not light oils and preparations: $2.7bn, growing 12%/yr","Cereals; rice, semi-milled or wholly milled, whether or not polished or glazed: $0.5bn, growing 21%/yr","Vegetable oils; palm oil and its fractions, other than crude, whether or not refined, but not chemically modified: $0.2bn, growing 45%/yr"]},{"headline":"Uganda, United Arab Emirates, United States take 29% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Uganda: 11.7% ($0.9bn)","United Arab Emirates: 9.4% ($0.8bn)","United States: 8.3% ($0.7bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 22% of what Kenya imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 21.5% ($4.3bn)","United Arab Emirates: 12.6% ($2.5bn)","India: 9.8% ($2.0bn)"]},{"headline":"2024 trade deficit of $11.9bn","detail":"Kenya buys more than it sells. Deficit economies can face foreign-exchange shortages, so check currency availability and payment terms before committing.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $8.3bn vs imports $20.2bn in 2024","Exports moved 15.3% year on year"]},{"headline":"Services are a real part of this economy","detail":"Commercial services exports are $8.0bn, about 7% of GDP. That usually signals working payment rails, English or lingua-franca business capability, and buyers already used to contracting across borders.","angle":"entry","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Services exports $8.0bn against GDP $120.4bn (2