ed: $0.2bn, growing 168%/yr","Iron or steel (excluding cast iron or stainless steel); seamless, line pipe of a kind used for oil or gas pipelines: $0.2bn, growing 49%/yr"]},{"headline":"China, India, Indonesia take 61% of exports","detail":"Export routes are narrow. Trade finance, shipping lanes and standards compliance are all built around these markets, which lowers your setup cost if you sell into them and raises it sharply if you do not.","angle":"partner","strength":"strong","evidence":["China: 43.8% ($14.5bn)","India: 11.0% ($3.6bn)","Indonesia: 5.9% ($2.0bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 21% of what Angola imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 20.9% ($3.4bn)","Portugal: 10.1% ($1.6bn)","India: 6.4% ($1.0bn)"]},{"headline":"2025 trade surplus of $16.9bn","detail":"Angola sells more than it buys. Surplus economies usually have foreign currency available, which makes getting paid and repatriating profit simpler.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $33.7bn vs imports $16.8bn in 2025","Exports moved -14.4% year on year"]},{"headline":"Early signal: tugs and pusher craft","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 62% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Transport equipment: growing 62% a year since 2022, now 0.54% of exports at rank 11. Largest counterpart across all exports is China. Growth is uneven, so treat the projection as directional."]}]','2026-09-06 10:18:32'),('res_940c7e575f5347c593b1c3','ent_cameroon','run_846af31cf50e4a579e044c','overview','{"year":2023,"export_usd":4967511895.978,"import_usd":8296875048.587,"balance_usd":-3329363152.609,"tot