 minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; not light oils and preparations, petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; light oils and preparations, vegetable oils; palm oil and its fractions, crude, not chemically modified","detail":"These are the fastest-growing things Cameroon buys from abroad. Rising imports mean domestic demand is outpacing domestic supply. That gap is either a place to sell into, or a place to produce locally and displace the import.","angle":"gap","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; not light oils and preparations: $1.1bn, growing 18%/yr","Petroleum oils and oils from bituminous minerals, not containing biodiesel, not crude, not waste oils; preparations n.e.c, containing by weight 70% or more of petroleum oils or oils from bituminous minerals; light oils and preparations: $0.8bn, growing 25%/yr","Vegetable oils; palm oil and its fractions, crude, not chemically modified: $0.2bn, growing 57%/yr"]},{"headline":"Netherlands, France, India take 47% of exports","detail":"Export destinations are reasonably spread, which means established routes and documentation for several markets rather than just one.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["Netherlands: 24.3% ($1.2bn)","France: 13.0% ($0.6bn)","India: 10.0% ($0.5bn)"]},{"headline":"Most imports arrive from China","detail":"China supplies 19% of what Cameroon imports. If you are sourcing to sell here, that is your incumbent competition and the price you have to beat. If you are buying, those trade lanes already exist.","angle":"partner","strength":"moderate","evidence":["China: 19.4% ($1.6bn)","India: 11.8% ($1.0bn)","France: 7.8% ($0.6bn)"]},{"headline":"2023 trade deficit of $3.3bn","detail":"Cameroon buys more than it sells. Deficit economies can face foreign-exchange shortages, so check currency availability and payment terms before committing.","angle":"risk","strength":"strong","evidence":["Exports $5.0bn vs imports $8.3bn in 2023","Exports moved -11.7% year on year"]},{"headline":"Early signal: cereals; rice, semi-milled or wholly milled, whether or not polished or glazed","detail":"Not a headline product yet, but growing 83% a year. Categories that hold that rate tend to reprice the market before they show up in the top ten, which is the window where entry is cheapest.","angle":"timing","strength":"strong","evidence":["Agriculture & food: growing 83% a year since 2020, now 0.41% of exports at rank 17. Largest counterpart across all exports is Netherlands. Growth is uneven, so treat the projection as directional."]}]','2026-09-06 10:18:33');
